Error [E-ERR-SIGIL]: `T ! E` and `T ? E` are retired infix fallible type spellings.
  --> tests/ui/retired_fallible_type_sigil.jet:3:12
    |
  3 | fn f() Int ! E -> Ok(1)
    |            ^
 Why: the success type and error type each have a clear suffix zone, so `?` keeps one meaning: possible absence.
 Fix: write `Entry? StoreError!`, `Int (DbError | TimeoutError)!`, or `IOError!`; write bare `!` for the default `Err` type.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E-ERR-SIGIL

